@startuml
' Figure 36.7  The finding lifecycle
' Reading order: top to bottom, F-0624-01 from June 24 to July 3, 2026.
' The owner moves the finding through containment, triage, the fix,
' and evidence; only the auditor opens and closes it, and she sends
' it back when the evidence does not hold. A later record that rebuts
' the claim sends it back to triage. From assurance.findings.
!include plantuml-theme.puml
hide empty description
[*] -right-> Opened : auditor
Opened -right-> Contained : owner
Contained -down-> Triaged : owner
Triaged -left-> FixLive : owner
FixLive -down-> Submitted : owner
Submitted -up-> FixLive : auditor,\nclaim fails
Submitted -right-> Closed : auditor
Closed -up-> Triaged : rebutted
@enduml
